    <string name="familie_perm_child_text">GateControl uses your precise location only when a parent of your family asks for it, or when you send “I’ve arrived” or an SOS. The position goes once to your family’s own GateControl server – to nobody else – and is deleted there after 7 days.</string>
    <string name="familie_perm_child_bg_text">Your parents get your location automatically. So that this also works while GateControl is closed or not in use, GateControl collects your location in the background – but only at the moment a parent asks, never continuously. On the next screen choose “Allow all the time”.</string>
    <string name="familie_perm_places_text">For place reminders GateControl uses your precise location on this phone to notice when you arrive at or leave a place you chose. The phone checks this itself; your location is not sent anywhere.</string>
    <string name="familie_perm_places_bg_text">Place reminders also work while GateControl is closed or not in use: GateControl collects your location in the background through Android’s geofencing for this. Only that a reminder fired is shared – and only when the reminder says so. On the next screen choose “Allow all the time”.</string>
    <string name="familie_places_info">Your phone checks the places itself. Your location is not sent for this – only the reminder, if you set it up that way.</string>
    <string name="familie_places_unavailable">Place reminders are not available on this device (it has no Google Play services). Reminders for you are listed but do not fire here.</string>
